{
	title: 'System-prompt change trail in the transcript',
	spec: 'When a file in a session\'s system prompt (SYSTEM.md, the files it includes, the AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md files for its cwd) changes, the session gets an output record with the change: file name (relative to the cwd when inside it), changed/added/removed, and a short diff (git diff -U1, headers dropped, at most 40 lines). The check runs before each prompt is recorded and before each provider round; the first check of a session only remembers (state in the session\'s prompt-files.json), and files that come or go with a cwd change are not reported. The model reads each record as a <meta> note in front of its next prompt, saying the user edited its instructions and earlier replies followed the old text, with the diff, so it does not mistake new rules for ones it ignored. Clients show consecutive change records as one card: one change heads as \'SYSTEM.md changed\'; several as \'3 changes to SYSTEM.md, AGENTS.md since 10:44\' (a date before the time if not today). On the web the card folds closed under that line and opens to each change\'s line and diff. The terminal draws it without a header: one change is one row ("11:25 AGENTS.md changed  +2 −0") with up to three changed lines in diff colours, or "blank lines only"; a run is one row ("11:14–11:25 3 changes to SYSTEM.md, AGENTS.md") and one aligned row per change: time, file, counts, its first changed line.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		"Records are output records with a change field (no new record type): replay turns them into notes, transcript.aside carries change, and promptChanges.group merges runs at draw time in both clients (web view.rows, terminal frame.layout), memoized per run so keyed rows and the terminal layout cache keep the object. Not hooked into prompts.amend: a replacing prompt would drop a record placed before it; the next round's check catches the edit."
	],
	needs: ['48']
